## Calibration done (vs W6 weights)

Only one change was needed; every AC-06 threshold already held with W6's weights (first measurement, before any change:
DIF-01 0 states; DIF-02 16/16; DIF-03 0 / 6 / noThreat 0; DIF-04 1.80/0.15/0.00; DIF-05 19/20/20, 7.35/5.70/3.10; DIF-06
209/209, 0; DIF-07 2.69/3.57/3.33 (pooled 2.57/3.63/3.37); OUT-04 16/20; OUT-05 6/20; OUT-07 0/20).
Gap found: TC-OUT-01 (frozen: AI-Empire activates in ≥ 10 of 13 rounds) FAILED for hard on 7/20 DIFF_SEEDS (9 rounds) — after
converging all its forces into the revealed base the hard Empire had nothing left to do and passed out rounds 10..13
(normal min was exactly 10). Fix (src/ai/empire-policy.ts + profiles.ts, new profile knob `cordon`): post-reveal "cordon" for
normal/hard — once the base is held (own ground there) and not pinned, ACTIVATE an empty neighbour of the base (0.3, below
converge 0.5/0.6 and assault 1.5/1.6, above PASS 0.05/0.01) and MOVE only the ships out (`ships-only`, 0.8; the ground never
leaves, so the base stays held); the next round the reinforcement (converge.base) brings them back. easy: cordon 0 (unchanged).
After: rounds with an AI activation — easy min 12, normal 13, hard 13 (all 20 seeds). Pre-reveal behaviour is untouched
(DIF-05/06/07 identical), the AI-Rebel side is untouched (DIF-01..04, OUT-04/05/07 identical, fixture seeds identical).
Plan deviation to accept (like W6 pull-forces): §4.5 has no post-reveal "cordon" row — recorded here, flagged in the report.

